title "O365 Platform (Run)"
layout row
subtitle "SaaS with On Prem/Cloud Exchange Servers and Active Directory"

# not modelled: legend, domain colour key, "Updated" date; undirected dashed
# lines chaining the three TMS boxes (Identity - App Mgmt - Compute)

BA o365: O365 E5
BA teams: Teams
BA sharepoint: SharePoint Online
BA exchange: Exchange
BA ad: Active Directory

SI teams-saas: Teams SaaS
SI sharepoint-saas: SharePoint SaaS
SI exchange-prod: Exchange Prod
SI exchange-dev: Exchange Dev
SI ad-prod: Active Directory 2022 Prod

BSO teams-bso: Teams
BSO sharepoint-sites: SharePoint Sites
BSO outlook: Outlook

BS messaging: Direct Messaging Services
BS file-sharing: File Sharing Services
BS email: Email Services

TMSO aad-admin: Azure Active Directory Administration
TMSO exchange-admin: Exchange Administration
TMSO windows-admin: Windows Server Admin

TMS identity: Identity Access Services
TMS app-mgmt: Application Mgmt Services
TMS compute: Compute Services

DCG windows-group: Windows Exchange Servers
CI(Application) exchange-app: Exchange
CI(Windows Server) windows: Exchange01, Exchange02

teams -> o365
sharepoint -> o365
exchange -> o365
teams -> teams-saas
sharepoint -> sharepoint-saas
exchange -> exchange-prod
# Exchange Prod is a stacked card with a "Dev" back card; Dev edges mirror the stack
exchange -> exchange-dev
ad -> ad-prod
teams-bso -> teams-saas
sharepoint-sites -> sharepoint-saas
outlook -> exchange-prod
teams-bso -> messaging
sharepoint-sites -> file-sharing
outlook -> email
aad-admin -> ad-prod
aad-admin -> identity
exchange-admin -> exchange-app
exchange-admin -> app-mgmt
windows-admin -> windows-group
windows-admin -> compute
windows-group -> windows
# the blue service-mapping connector starts at the Dev back card and runs behind
# Application Exchange to the Windows servers stack; read as the stack -> app -> servers
exchange-prod -> exchange-app
exchange-dev -> exchange-app
exchange-app -> windows
# "Sends Data to" is one dash-dot connector glued to Teams SaaS that runs up the
# instance column behind Exchange Prod and SharePoint SaaS; read as all three
ad-prod -> teams-saas : Sends Data to
ad-prod -> sharepoint-saas : Sends Data to
ad-prod -> exchange-prod : Sends Data to
